Subject: [PATCH] compulab: dts: Match PCIe ports to GBE UPHY config 9

Edge-AI selects gbe-uphy-config-9 in ODMDATA. This routes GBE lane 0 to
C7 and lane 1 to C9 as independent x1 root ports. The reference carrier
configuration still assigns both lanes to C7 and inherits its SoC lane
count. The earlier Edge-AI patch also enables C9 and C10 without supplying
their PHY mappings, causing the PCIe driver to reject their device trees.

Describe C7 and C9 as x1 ports with their respective PHYs. Leave C10
disabled: it is not exposed as a general-purpose PCIe port on Orin NX/Nano.
Keep these settings in the carrier DTS rather than the shared SoC DTS.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CompuLab Edge-AI carrier configuration]
---
 .../nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi | 22 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hardware/nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi b/hardware/nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi
--- a/hardware/nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi
+++ b/hardware/nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi
@@ -205,13 +205,29 @@
 		};
 
-		/* C7 - M.2 Key-M */
+		/* GBE UPHY config 9: C7 x1 on lane 0, C9 x1 on lane 1. */
 		pcie@141e0000 {
 			status = "okay";
+			num-lanes = <1>;
 
 			vddio-pex-ctl-supply = <&vdd_1v8_ao>;
 
-			phys = <&p2u_gbe_0>, <&p2u_gbe_1>;
-			phy-names = "p2u-0", "p2u-1";
+			phys = <&p2u_gbe_0>;
+			phy-names = "p2u-0";
+		};
+
+		pcie@140c0000 {
+			status = "okay";
+			num-lanes = <1>;
+
+			vddio-pex-ctl-supply = <&vdd_1v8_ao>;
+
+			phys = <&p2u_gbe_1>;
+			phy-names = "p2u-0";
+		};
+
+		/* C10 is not a general-purpose PCIe port on Orin NX/Nano. */
+		pcie@140e0000 {
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 	};
 
